        "original_id": "fc1295ca-f61b-5ce9-b54d-2f7ca1be7a04",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Leeds, Yorkshire's West Riding, West Yorkshire, England\n- Organizations: Kingdom of Elmet\n- Concepts: Elmet\n- Products: St John's Centre\n\nFacts:\n- In the 5th century, the name Leeds referred to a wooded area of the Kingdom of Elmet.\n- Elmet was an independent Brittonic kingdom from about the 5th century to the early 7th century.\n- Elmet was an area of what later became the West Riding of Yorkshire.\n- Historically, Leeds was in Yorkshire's West Riding.\n- St John's Centre is an indoor shopping centre in Leeds, West Yorkshire, England.",
